# The behavior snapshots record each fixture component's size_bytes, so a
# fixture's byte count is part of the frozen behavior. Under a global
# core.autocrlf=true the checkout carries CRLF, inflating every size_bytes by
# one byte per line — snapshots regenerated on such a checkout then disagree
# with any LF checkout, and continuous integration fails the whole corpus.
# Pin the working copy to LF so the recorded sizes are checkout-independent.
* text=auto eol=lf
